    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d487-a1">

                <pb facs="0846" n="1804" xml:id="pg1804"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">memorandum</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-03-07"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 7,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Canadian sealers seem required to carry appeal to United States court, or by
                    failure to do that will forfeit bonds. Can they be allowed to bond vessels and
                    skins, without obligation to appeal and pending definite settlement between
                    United States and Great Britain?</p>
            </div>
        </body>
